+# Implementer Brief 12: Wire Real Dog Identity, Fix Action Bar Unmount & Align Lifecycle
+
+## Context & Objectives
+Address all Cycle 3 reviewer findings:
+1. Real companion dog identity from `clifton_walker_profile` / `SocialHUD` wired into `HomeSanctuary` and `HomeFeeding`.
+2. Do not destroy `#home-action-bar` on `HomeFeeding.unmount()`; preserve the container element and only clear children / event listeners.
+3. `updateDisabledState()` in `home_feeding.js` strictly disables `#btn-action-feed` when `dogSlot === null`.
+4. In `social_hud.js`: opening Home with a dog present defaults to `'sanctuary'`; adopting a dog resets active tab to `'walker'`.
+5. Comprehensive unit tests covering mount -> unmount -> remount and real profile integration.
+
+## Detailed Requirements
+
+### 1. `virtual_dog_walker/src/ui/home_sanctuary.js`
+- In `readProfile()`:
+  Read `localStorage.getItem('clifton_walker_profile')`.
+  If found, parse JSON. Extract `profile.dogSlot` (or `profile.dogName`, `profile.coatKey`, `profile.collarColor`).
+  If `profile.dogSlot === null`, return `null`.
+  If active profile has a dog, resolve the appearance using `dogSlot.coatKey` or `dogSlot.name`.
+- In `mount(canvasEl, explicitDogSlot)`:
+  Accept optional `explicitDogSlot` override. If provided, use it. Otherwise call `readProfile()`.
+  If dog slot is present, initialize the companion dog with the real name and coat:
+  `dog.name = dogSlot.name || 'Ziggy';`
+  `dog.id = dogSlot.id || 'dog-1';`
+- Expose `getDogSlot()` on `window.HomeSanctuary`:
+  ```javascript
+  getDogSlot: function () {
+    return activeDogSlot;
+  }
+  ```
+
+### 2. `virtual_dog_walker/src/ui/home_feeding.js`
+- In `getDogSlot()`:
+  Query `window.HomeSanctuary?.getDogSlot?.()`.
+  If `window.HomeSanctuary` has `getDogSlot`, return its result.
+  Only if `HomeSanctuary` is not mounted, check `window.__vdwActiveDogSlot` or `clifton_walker_profile`. Never assume a dog exists just because the canvas element exists!
+- In `updateDisabledState()`:
+  If `getDogSlot() === null`, `#btn-action-feed` must be `disabled = true;`.
+- In `unmount()`:
+  Do NOT remove `actionBarEl` from its parent!
+  Instead, clear its children and listeners:
+  ```javascript
+  if (feedBtnEl && feedBtnEl.__homeFeedingBound) {
+    feedBtnEl.removeEventListener('click', onFeedClick);
+    feedBtnEl.__homeFeedingBound = false;
+  }
+  if (actionBarEl) {
+    actionBarEl.innerHTML = '';
+  }
+  feedBtnEl = null;
+  ```
+- In `ensureActionBar()`:
+  First query `document.getElementById('home-action-bar')`. If it exists, use it! Only create if missing.
+
+### 3. `virtual_dog_walker/src/ui/social_hud.js`
+- In `openModal()`:
+  When `this.dogSlot !== null`:
+  Default to `this.setHomeView('sanctuary');` when opening.
+- When saving/adopting a dog in `handleSaveDog()` / `adoptDogFromForm()`:
+  - `this.isHomeLocked = false;`
+  - Switch tab back to `'walker'`: `this.switchTab('walker');`
+  - Set `this.setHomeView('sanctuary');`
+- In `setHomeView()` when mounting sanctuary:
+  Pass `this.dogSlot` to `window.HomeSanctuary?.mount?.(canvas, this.dogSlot);`
+  and set `window.__vdwActiveDogSlot = this.dogSlot;`
+
+### 4. Tests (`test_home_sanctuary.py` & `test_home_menu.py`)
+- Add test in `test_home_sanctuary.py`:
+  - `test_exec_mount_unmount_remount_preserves_action_bar_in_sanctuary`:
+    Mount sanctuary and feeding, unmount, remount. Assert `#home-action-bar` remains child of `#home-view-sanctuary`.
+  - `test_exec_real_profile_identity_used_in_feed_and_toast`:
+    Seed `clifton_walker_profile` with `{ name: 'Walker', dogSlot: { name: 'Barnaby', coatKey: 'GOLDEN' } }`.
+    Mount and click feed, assert toast contains `"Barnaby loved the meal! ❤️"` and persisted `last_feed_at` has valid dog info.
+  - `test_exec_feed_disabled_when_dog_slot_is_null`:
+    Seed with `dogSlot: null`, mount, assert feed button is disabled.
+
+## Verification
+`python3 -m unittest test/test_home_sanctuary.py test/test_home_menu.py`
+All tests must pass (0 failures, 0 errors).
+
+
